Hi August,

On 10/07/2015 09:44, August Mayer wrote:
> Hello everybody,
>
> Which modems are supported well by ofono, in your experience?
>
> We are currently evaluating modems, and we would like to know which
> modems cooperate well with ofono. We are interested in modems which
> support a GPRS/UMTS data connection, and voice calls and SMS messaging
> for some use cases; dual-SIM support would also be useful.
>
> We are integrating the modems into our hardware, in various use cases
> in an automotive context, and we use modem modules with integrated RF
> support, so I'm not so much interested about USB sticks or PCI cards.
> But feel free to share your observations anyway!
>
> Many thanks & greetings          August
>

Cinterion EHS6 is working well for us with data. I can't speak to
voice/SMS at present but this is on my roadmap and I'd be interested in
putting any needed time in to prove this out. Historically we've found
the module itself pretty reliable and the support from Cinterion/Gemalto
excellent.

Regards,

Alex

